Introduction
------------
PAN accelerates packets between any two linux RVU interfaces.
PAN supports acceleraton of both L2 and L3 traffic. Please ensure
that all interfaces in network topology are cavium devices for
PAN to accelerate. Below shows various topologies that can be
accelerated with PAN.
note: We used sdp1-0 and eth0 in example configuration. User is
free to choose any cavium netdevices.

1. Kernel Config
CONFIG_OCTEONTX_PAN=m

2. How to Build
make ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-marvell-linux-gnu- modules  -j16 V=s

3. L2 offload - Linux bridge FDB based.

                         cn10k
 |-------|         |--------------|                |-------
 | x86   |---------|sdp1-0   eth0 |----------------| x86  |
 |       |         |      br0     |                |      |
 ---------         |--------------                 --------
 192.168.9.200                                     192.168.9.100

3.a) configuration

insmod ./pcie-marvell-cnxk-ep.ko

./octep_cp_agent ./cn106xx.cfg 2>&1 > /tmp/octep-cp-log.txt &

brctl addbr br0
ifconfig sdp1-0 up
ifconfig eth0 up
brctl addif br0 eth0
brctl addif br0 sdp1-0
insmod ./pan.ko

ifconfig pan up

devlink dev eswitch set pci/0002:1c:00.0 mode switchdev

ifconfig br0 up
mount -t debugfs none /sys/kernel/debug/

4.  L3 offload - Route Table based

pros:
Less number of NPC mcam rules used.
cons:
No masquerade support)

4.1 Simple routing

                         cn10k
 |-------|         |------------------------ |                |-------
 | x86   |---------|sdp1-0           eth0    |----------------| x86  |
 |       |         |192.168.11.1  192.168.9.1|                |      |
 ---------         |-------------------------                 --------
 192.168.11.200                                            192.168.9.100

4.1.a) configuration
insmod ./pcie-marvell-cnxk-ep.ko

./octep_cp_agent ./cn106xx.cfg 2>&1 > /tmp/octep-cp-log.txt &

ifconfig sdp1-0 192.168.11.1 up
ifconfig eth0 192.168.9.1 up
insmod ./pan.ko

ifconfig pan up

devlink dev eswitch set pci/0002:1c:00.0 mode switchdev

mount -t debugfs none /sys/kernel/debug/
echo 1 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward

4.2 Bridge + route

                         cn10k
 |-------|         |------------------------ |                |-------
 | x86   |---------|sdp1-0          br0 (eth0)|----------------| x86  |
 |       |         |192.168.11.1  192.168.9.1|                |      |
 ---------         |-------------------------                 --------
 192.168.11.200                                            192.168.9.100

4.2.a configuration

insmod ./pcie-marvell-cnxk-ep.ko

./octep_cp_agent ./cn106xx.cfg 2>&1 > /tmp/octep-cp-log.txt &

ifconfig sdp1-0 192.168.11.1 up
brctl addbr br0
brctl addif br0 eth0
ifconfig eth0 up
insmod ./pan.ko

ifconfig pan up

devlink dev eswitch set pci/0002:1c:00.0 mode switchdev

mount -t debugfs none /sys/kernel/debug/
echo 1 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward
ifconfig br0 192.168.9.1 up

4.2 two Bridge + route

                         cn10k
 |-------|         |------------------------ |                |-------
 | x86   |---------|br1(sdp1-0)    br0 (eth0)|----------------| x86  |
 |       |         |192.168.11.1  192.168.9.1|                |      |
 ---------         |-------------------------                 --------
 192.168.11.200                                            192.168.9.100

4.2.a configuration

insmod ./pcie-marvell-cnxk-ep.ko

./octep_cp_agent ./cn106xx.cfg 2>&1 > /tmp/octep-cp-log.txt &

brctl addbr br0
brctl addif br0 eth0
ifconfig eth0 up

brctl addbr br1
brctl addif br1 sdp1-0
ifconfig sdp1-0 up
insmod ./pan.ko

ifconfig pan up

ifconfig br0 192.168.9.1 up
ifconfig br1 192.168.11.1 up

devlink dev eswitch set pci/0002:1c:00.0 mode switchdev

mount -t debugfs none /sys/kernel/debug/
echo 1 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward

5. L3 support - Flow based (https://docs.kernel.org/networking/nf_flowtable.html)
pros:
Various masquerading can be supported. Currently only SNAT and DNAT for ipv4 is supported.
cons:
NF table offload configuration should be enabled in Kernel.
Each flow creates two mcam entries. one for original direction and other for reply.
We need to disable route Table based flow offload by writing 0 to a sysfs entry, as below.
echo 0 > /sys/kernel/debug/cn10k/pan/sw_mode

5.a) Simple routing
                         cn10k
 |-------|         |------------------------ |                |-------
 | x86   |---------|sdp1-0           eth0    |----------------| x86  |
 |       |         |192.168.11.1  192.168.9.1|                |      |
 ---------         |-------------------------                 --------
 192.168.11.200                                            192.168.9.100

insmod ./pcie-marvell-cnxk-ep.ko

./octep_cp_agent ./cn106xx.cfg 2>&1 > /tmp/octep-cp-log.txt &

ifconfig sdp1-0 192.168.11.1 up
ifconfig eth0 192.168.9.1 up
insmod ./pan.ko
mount -t debugfs none /sys/kernel/debug/
echo 0 > /sys/kernel/debug/cn10k/pan/sw_mode

ifconfig pan up

devlink dev eswitch set pci/0002:1c:00.0 mode switchdev

echo 1 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward
nft -f ./route.nft

++++++++ ./route.nft ++++
table inet x {

     flowtable f {
        hook ingress priority 0
        devices = { eth0, sdp1-0 }
        flags offload;
     }

    chain forward {
        type filter hook forward priority 0; policy accept;
        ct state { established, related } flow add @f
    }
}
+++++++++++++++++++++++++

5.b)  ROUTE + BRIDGE

                         cn10k
 |-------|         |------------------------ |                |-------
 | x86   |---------|sdp1-0          br0 (eth0)|----------------| x86  |
